<title>ANTIGUA: CRICKET-RAIN CASTS DOUBT OVER 2ND DAY'S PLAY IN TEST.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RAIN CASTS DOUBT OVER 2ND DAY'S PLAY IN TEST.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOHN'S, Antigua 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Play on the second day of the fourth test between West Indies and India seemed doubtful after heavy early rain on Saturday.</p>
<p>There were several pools of water on the outfield at the Antigua Recreation Ground where similar conditions after morning showers prevented play on Friday's scheduled opening day.</p>
<p>West Indies lead the five-test series 1-0 after winning the third test in Bridgetown, Barbados, by 38 runs.</p>
